* Monroe's Motivated Sequence
Is a sequeme or an order for a persuasive speech, is effective because it was designed on human psychology.

It is divided in five stages
- Attention: It consists of four elements (Thesis, Hook, Credibility, Relevance) and before it continues to the next points it has a preview.
- Need: Prof said it needs to provide an statement, an explanation
- Satisfaction
- Visualization
- Call to Action

  
